From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: verify-vendoring: recognise riscv64 binaries

The ELF sanity check only matches `file`'s output for x86-64 and aarch64, so
it fails a riscv64 binary that is otherwise fine:

    FAIL: Unexpected binary type: ELF 64-bit LSB pie executable, UCB RISC-V, ...

Add a branch for `file`'s "RISC-V" architecture string.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [only needed once a riscv64 leg exists to call this script; upstream's own x86_64/aarch64 legs never hit this path]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/ci/verify-vendoring.sh b/ci/verify-vendoring.sh
--- a/ci/verify-vendoring.sh
+++ b/ci/verify-vendoring.sh
@@ -128,6 +128,8 @@
     pass "Binary is ELF 64-bit x86-64"
 elif echo "$FILE_TYPE" | grep -q "ELF 64-bit.*aarch64"; then
     pass "Binary is ELF 64-bit aarch64"
+elif echo "$FILE_TYPE" | grep -q "ELF 64-bit.*RISC-V"; then
+    pass "Binary is ELF 64-bit RISC-V"
 else
     fail "Unexpected binary type: $FILE_TYPE"
 fi
